## Before working

- Use the "Verification checklist" and "Test approach" structure in `docs/workflow/DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md`.
- Keep §3 test case list and §5 test results format per `docs/template/REQUIREMENT_TEMPLATE.md`.

## Gate: build and restart before verification

Only run verification **after** build and restart are confirmed. If the handoff from Frontend/Backend does **not** include a clear "Build: … exit N. Restart: … done" (or equivalent), **run the appropriate build and restart yourself** (e.g. `./scripts/dev-services.sh frontend restart` or `backend restart` from project root), then run verification. Do **not** ask the user to run restart; the QA subagent performs it. Only if you cannot run the script (e.g. no terminal), ask the user to have Frontend/Backend complete build and restart and hand off again.

This avoids verifying against a stale or unbuilt state. See `docs/workflow/SUBAGENT-DELEGATION.md` §2.1.

## After build and restart (verification)

When **Frontend or Backend** have completed **build and restart** (confirmed in handoff or by you), **QA performs verification**:

1. Run verification per `.cursor/commands/verify.md` (restart + health check: backend 9200, frontend 3001). **When the change includes frontend** and a **browser MCP** is available, **you must run step 3.5** (browser check): open http://localhost:3001, capture page, run §3 and (if present) §3.5 browser procedures; produce a **detailed report** (see below). Policy: `docs/workflow/BROWSER-AUTOMATION-VERIFICATION-POLICY.md`. **Browser step 3.5**: **Default (preferred)**: **AgentDeskAI** (user-browser-tools) — use `takeScreenshot`, `runAccessibilityAudit`, `runPerformanceAudit`, `runSEOAudit` when available (requires Chrome extension + `npx @agentdeskai/browser-tools-server@latest` in a terminal). For navigate/click/fill flows, use **puppeteer_*** or **cursor-ide-browser** (navigate → lock → snapshot, never lock before navigate); wait 2–3 s after navigate before snapshot; if snapshot has no refs, wait and retry. Record in §5 which tool was used and any skip reason (no MCP / no refs / screenshot timeout). Troubleshooting: `docs/workflow/QA-BROWSER-TEST-TROUBLESHOOTING.md`.
2. Update requirement doc **§5** (test results); for error fixes also **§6** (Error remedy result). **Detailed report for browser verification**: tool used, base URL; per-TC Pass/Fail and short note; for each **Fail** include what was checked (selector/ref), expected, actual so Frontend can fix.
3. **On verification failure (any scope)**: Do **not** commit. Create a **bugfix child** (`docs/requirements/{parentID}-bugfix-{N}.md`), describe the failure and **identify failure scope** (frontend | backend | db | security | contract | ux | …). **Always hand off to Requirements** (never directly to Frontend, Backend, or other implementer). Requirements formalizes the doc and **delegates to the responsible expert** by scope (Frontend, Backend, DB, Security, Contract, UX→Frontend, etc.). When the expert **closes** the issue (fix + build/restart), they hand off to **QA**; QA **re-runs verification**. When **all** issues are closed and verification passes → commit.
4. **Commit** (only when all checks pass) per `.cursor/commands/commit-on-complete.md`. If the user requested push, run `git push` after the commit; otherwise do not push.
5. Hand off to Documentation/Release or Done per `docs/workflow/AGENT-COLLABORATION-ON-REQUIREMENT.md` Step 5 → 6.

## Collaboration

- On requirement-driven work: **Step 5** in `docs/workflow/AGENT-COLLABORATION-ON-REQUIREMENT.md`. Input: requirement doc §3, implemented feature, and **confirmation that build and restart are done**. Output: verification (per verify.md), §5 (and §6 for error fixes), and **commit** per `.cursor/commands/commit-on-complete.md`. The main agent does not commit when delegation is in effect.

